### 7.1 Inspected Protocol Exchanges

Wireshark inspection has identified:

- Gateway-to-backend HTTP readiness probes.
- Gateway-to-backend `/users/` requests.
- Backend HTTP 200 responses.
- Backend-to-PostgreSQL TCP communication.
- TCP connection and reset events.
- Continued readiness responses from Backend B.
- Successful readiness responses from Backend A after restart.

The failure/recovery capture includes a readiness request to Backend A followed by an HTTP 200 response. Subsequent application requests to Backend A are also visible.

Gateway logs and status information provide complementary evidence of the backend health-state transitions.

